        "body": "Related: #105736\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe enforced production-mode Knip ratchet still carried unused export surface across the Discord and QA Lab plugins. Test-only consumers also kept several production exports alive without a runtime caller.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nRemoves 21 stale baseline entries and rehomes four QA Lab test controls under the canonical testing surfaces. Contract entry files remain untouched; all Telegram changes were removed to keep #106153 exclusively owned and conflict-free.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior change. Plugin internals expose less accidental API surface, and the dead-export baseline shrinks by 17 net entries.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports:update`: regenerated immediately before the rewritten push; 3,289 entries.\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports`: matched all 3,289 entries on Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxdgm4zhgymh8r8205b2hsbt`.\n- `pnpm test extensions/discord`: 171 files, 2,034 tests passed.\n- `pnpm test extensions/qa-lab`: 104 files and 1,464 tests passed; three failures remain in two untouched tests with current-main fixture/output drift.\n- `pnpm tsgo:extensions`: touched plugins passed; latest-main run reaches the unrelated untouched `extensions/msteams/src/attachments/html.ts` unused-helper error.\n- Autoreview: clean on the final 43k Discord + QA Lab branch bundle; no accepted or actionable findings.\n- Scope audit: Telegram tree is byte-identical to `origin/main`; no configured contract entry changed.\n",
